Proxmox authentication on generic controller paths
=================================================

Generic discovery and the shared controller adapter factory now carry stored
Proxmox token IDs, decrypted token secrets and configured realms. The later
deep-sync adapter receives the same options. API-token preference over ticket
login, encrypted and legacy plaintext credentials, and default pam behavior
match the existing controller connection tests. No vendor registry expansion
or change to hypervisor inventory ownership is included.

Qualification exercises the actual Proxmox adapter/client and PostgreSQL
against synthetic protocol peers. It does not establish new live hardware
compatibility or modify a Proxmox node. Generic discovery still excludes
hypervisor nodes from network inventory; the hypervisor module owns them.
Provider discovery error propagation, ticket/connection cache authority,
malformed legacy secret handling, background caller grants and concurrent
post-check effects remain separate reviews.
